A '''vibro-ax''',<ref name="DB" /> or '''vibro-axe''',<ref name="Smuggler's Run">''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]''</ref> was a type of [[Axe|ax]] that used a compact generator to create vibrations along the cutting edge's surface, which significantly increased the weapon's lethality.<ref name="DB" /> There existed one-handed<ref name="BTA" /> and two-handed models.<ref name="ROTJ" /> Similar [[Vibro-weapon|vibration-based technology]] could be found in [[Vibroblade|vibro-blades]], [[Vibroknife|vibro-knives]],<ref name="Smuggler's Run" /> [[vibro-pike]]s,<ref name="aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> and [[vibro-lance]]s.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>

Vibro-axes were wielded by many thugs across [[the galaxy]]. The [[pig]]-like [[Gamorrean]]s, for example, often used them.<ref name="DB" /> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], some Gamorrean [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] favored a particular model of vibro-ax known as [[Arg'garok]]<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref>

[[Bounty hunter]] [[Ketsu Onyo]] owned a [[Ketsu's staff|staff]] that was equipped with a vibro-ax on the end of it for close-range combat.<ref name="BS">{{Rebels|Blood Sisters}}</ref>

The [[Weequay]] [[Pagetti Rook]] wielded a [[BD-1 Cutter vibro-ax]] during his service under [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]].<ref name="ROTJ" />

The [[Knights of Ren|Knight of Ren]] member [[Ap'lek]] carried a [[Mandalorian]] vibro-ax called the [[munit'kad halberd]], as his primary weapon.<ref name="TROS:TVD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

The bounty hunter [[Ax Tagrin]] owned a collapsible vibro-ax that he used on several occasions. It could break open doors, charge up with energy, be thrown as a [[weapon]] and used in [[Melee weapon|melee]] encounters.<ref name="The Missing Agent">{{Resistance|The Missing Agent}}</ref>

